    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2025/01/hoka-clifton-10-review-2025.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The Clifton 10 has ample underfoot protection but a firmer, less compliant CM-EVA feel than prior versions; the new 8 mm drop makes the heel feel higher, with a firmer heel and slightly firm forefoot.",
        "Responsiveness: The rocker plus firmer foam gives decent forward roll and mildly snappy toe-off, but bounce/energy return is moderate and the shoe is not especially quick.",
        "Stability: Stability is neutral with gentle guidance from sidewalls/flare; midfoot feels more stable from the firmer platform, and heel hold is strong with a rigid, well-padded heel counter (with some initial lateral stiffness before break-in).",
        "Durability: Outsole longevity is a weak point, with notable wear/ripping of outsole and exposed midsole reported around 30 miles; overall durability is below-average to average, while midsole firmness holds up reasonably well."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2025/01/hoka-clifton-10-multi-tester-review-big.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: Clifton 10 delivers comfortable, protective cushioning with a higher heel stack and 8 mm drop; the heel feels firmer at first (not mushy), while forefoot cushioning stays similar and the ride smooths after break-in.",
        "Responsiveness: Testers consistently found limited energy return and snappiness; the EVA midsole feels less bouncy/rebounding than newer supercritical foams, with only a small improvement after a few runs.",
        "Stability: Stability is notably improved via the wider platform, rear Active Foot Frame geometry, dense EVA, and rigid heel counter/stiff rear collar, giving stronger medial/lateral support but an initially over-rigid rear feel.",
        "Durability: This excerpt provides little direct evidence on outsole wear or long-term material longevity, so durability conclusions are limited."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Believe in the Run",
      "priority": 5,
      "url": "https://believeintherun.com/shoe-reviews/hoka-clifton-10-review/",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The Clifton 10 keeps a plush underfoot feel with very soft collar/heel padding, while the CMEVA midsole is balanced rather than overly squishy; the move to an 8 mm drop/additional heel stack was specifically aimed at improving heel cushioning under long-term impact.",
        "Responsiveness: Ride feel is described as fairly responsive with smooth turnover/transition and a \"touch\" of pop, but not a highly bouncy or snappy super-shoe style response.",
        "Stability: Heel hold is solid (bulbous heel counter, secure lacing, no heel lift/hotspots), suggesting dependable daily-trainer stability; explicit torsional rigidity/lateral support metrics were not detailed.",
        "Durability: Early wear feedback is strong (midsole still feels fresh after ~40 miles), and the Durabrasion rubber outsole is called out for durable placement and reliable traction in high-wear zones."
      ]
    }
  ],
